          <td style="border-bottom: 0px; border-left: 0px; border-right: 0px; border-top: 1.0pt solid #000000; padding: 3pt 2pt 2pt 2pt; vertical-align: top; width: 230.31pt" colspan="3">
                        <p class="CellBody">The main facade of the building has a small setback from the property line. The resulting front yard is typically very small and may be undefined or defined by a fence or hedge to spatially maintain the edge of the street. An integral porch is open on one, two, or three sides and is part of the overall massing and roof form of the building, making it impossible to remove the porch without major changes to the overall roof form.</p>

